            <ArticleTitle>Gradual resolution of an arachnoid cyst after spontaneous rupture into the subdural space. Case report.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1085-6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The authors present the case of a young patient in whom the spontaneous rupture of a known, long-standing middle fossa arachnoid cyst into the subdural space was documented. This spontaneous rupture was followed by gradual diminution of the cyst to near-complete resolution.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
